notes: "This is the part of HUANDENG that comes most directly from the story-first idea. Every slide carries a short Story: what it is for, what must be kept, and what change was asked for. Think of it as an alignment tool between me and the agent. On the left is the Story tab in the Inspector, for the 1BNA slide; on the right, the same Story at a readable size. Keep the exact values, keep the labelled axis and its units, keep the citation, make no claims of replicates or trends, and never retouch the figure. The change came from my own feedback while preparing this talk: data plots should be drawn with a professional tool such as a Python package, from the data, not built inside the slide. Charts drawn inside slides are one of the strongest sources of the AI look. The request says what to change and, just as important, what must not move. When an agent works on that slide, it reads this first. Story also exists for the whole project, each Section and each Presentation. An agent’s Story is its interpretation, not my approval."
